*DESCRIPTION_START
The roots of the giant alder weave their skein in a dizzying pattern of 
latticework which thrusts deep into the rich soil all around you. This 
subterranean hollow lays directly beneath the trunk of the great alder. A 
circular fire pit rests in the precise center of the chamber. The only 
obvious egress would be to climb through the tangle of roots back into 
the boughs of the tree.
*DESCRIPTION_END
